    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T10:38:15Z",
    "body": "Probe result: this is not a sim bug and not a carry bug. The slivers are true rest material.\n\n1. The tool is `EM-0600-4FL`. It is a 6 mm end mill (`diameter: 6.0` in the catalog), not a 0.6 in (15.24 mm) end mill.\n2. The posted path around each corner is an arc of radius 3 mm about the part corner. For example: `(-25, -28) -> (-28, -25)`, center `(-25, -25)`. The XY extents of the path are -28..28.\n3. The swept tool disc therefore covers every point within 6 mm of the part corner. The stock corner is 5 * sqrt(2) = 7.07 mm from the part corner. In each 5 x 5 corner square, the area outside the 6 mm quarter disc stays at full height. Its legs are 5 - sqrt(11) = 1.68 mm, and its area is 1.227 mm^2.\n4. The carried body (`incoming_body` for the flipped Setup2, cell 0.375 mm) keeps 40 full-height brim columns, 10 at each corner. All of them are 6.02 mm to 6.81 mm from the part corner. No full-height column is inside the swept disc.\n5. With `EM-0800-4FL` (reach 8 mm > 7.07 mm), the carried body keeps no full-height brim column.\n\nThe carried body agrees with the geometry, so no code change is necessary. A pinning suite, `crates/app/tests/carried_corner_rest.rs`, checks both cases column by column. The decision is in `docs/decisions/1551-corner-sliver-true-rest.md`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
